Hi Marc,

What you meant makes perfect sense and is very clear now that I come back and review everything with a clear mind, thank you for the additional clarification. My apologies--my brain has been a bit inundated with lots of different sources of information these days so it's not hard for me to find myself a bit turned around!

Ok, so I think I see how this would work. So there would then basically be three different intercept terms (indicated by the alphas), one for each linear regression (for each forest level category)? I don't know if I have that quite right. I may be overthinking it, but especially with the inclusion of these alpha terms, I am a little unsure of how to incorporate this into the current model structure I have now. I also wasn't entirely clear on the difference between the logit linear regression on psi vs theta, as I have psi in my model.

 So I have my MSOM with species-specific random effects [indexed by k], DA, a detection covariate, as well as continuous standardized forest cover and fragmentation covariates on occupancy I'd also like to incorporate if possible. I also have a correlation matrix for detection and occupancy, and wanted to derive Nsite (richness per site) and N for the metacommunity. This may be too many parameters to include at once--but for now just to show, this is my guess at setting up the model incorporating the specification you provided above. Any insight on whether this appears to be a correct way to specify this would be very appreciated!:

model{
  for(k in 1:M){  # Loop through species
    w[k] ~ dbern(omega)

    # Likelihood
    for(i in 1:nSites) {
       # Ecological model
      logit(psi[i, k]) <- b0[k] + bFor[k] * forest[i] + bED[k] * frag[i]   #bED is continuous edge density fragmentation covariate; bFor is continuous forest cover covariate
      + alowfor[k] * low[i] + blowfor[k] * low[i] * frag[i] #Logit linear regression of psi on fragmentation in sites with low forest cover
      + amedfor[k] * medium[i] + bmedfor[k] * medium[i] * frag[i] #Logit linear regression of psi on fragmentation in sites with medium forest cover
      + ahighfor[k] * high[i] + bhighfor[k] * high[i] * frag[i] #Logit linear regression of psi on fragmentation in sites with high forest cover
       z[i, k] ~ dbern(psi[i, k] * w[k])
       # Observation model
       logit(p[i, k]) <- a0[k] + aTrail[k] * trail[i]  #effect of camera trap on/off trail on species detection
       y[i, k] ~ dbin(p[i, k] * z[i, k], nOcc[i]) #n0cc = # of occasions per site
    }

    # Priors (species level)/species heterogeneity
    b0[k] ~ dnorm(mu.b0, tau.b0).         #measure of correlation between detection and occupancy
    mu.eta[k] <- mu.a0 + rho * sd.a0/sd.b0 *
        (b0[k] - mu.b0)
    a0[k] ~ dnorm(mu.eta[k], tau.eta)

    alowfor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.alow, tau.alow)
    amedfor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.amedium, tau.amedium)
    ahighfor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.ahigh, tau.ahigh)
    bFor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.bforest, tau.bforest)
    bED[k] ~ dnorm(mu.frag, tau.frag)
    blowfor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.lowfor, tau.lowfor)
    bmedfor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.medfor, tau.medfor)
    bhighfor[k] ~ dnorm(mu.highfor, tau.highfor)

    aTrail[k]~ dnorm(mu.atrail, tau.atrail)
  }

  # Hyperpriors (community level)
  omega ~ dbeta(0.001, 1) #Link's scale prior

## for occupancy
#intercepts
  mu.b0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.b0 ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.b0 <- 1/sd.b0^2

#forest level indicator intercept terms
  mu.alow  ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.alow ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.alow <- 1/sd.alow^2
  mu.amedium  ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.amedium ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.amedium <- 1/sd.amedium^2
  mu.ahigh  ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.ahigh ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.ahigh <- 1/sd.ahigh^2

  mu.bforest ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.bforest ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.bforest <- 1/sd.bforest^2
  mu.frag ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.frag ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.frag <- 1/sd.frag^2
  mu.lowfor ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.lowfor ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.lowfor <- 1/sd.lowfor^2
  mu.medfor ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.medfor ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.medfor <- 1/sd.medfor^2
  mu.highfor ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.highfor ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.highfor <- 1/sd.medfor^2

##for detection
  mu.a0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.a0 ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.a0 <- 1/sd.a0^2

  mu.atrail ~ dnorm(0, 0.2)
  sd.atrail ~ dunif(-10, 5)
  tau.atrail <- 1/sd.atrail^2

  rho ~ dunif(-1, 1)
  tau.eta <- tau.a0/(1 - rho^2)

  # Derived quantities
  for(i in 1:nSites) {
  Nsite[i] <- sum(z[i,]) #richness per site
  }
  N <- sum(w)                 # Total metacommunity size

}

Thanks again for contributing to what I realize is a very length and complex discussion! All of your help as been sincerely appreciated.

Best,

Jordan

